    <text>Agreed on all seven. One placement question needs your call before I make changes.

**1. Three children: no, the tree doesn't support it.** [garden.js:142-166](garden.js#L142-L166) only handles 1 or 2 children. A third child is silently not drawn at all. `lost_in_conv` already has DELEGATE52 and UserLM, so there are two options:
- **(a) Recommended:** make it a child of `delegate52`, which has no children yet, and add an indirect link back to `lost_in_conv`. Long-horizon delegation leading to evolving intent over long interactions is a believable lineage, and the dotted line keeps the Lost in Conversation connection visible.
- **(b)** Extend garden.js to draw three children in a fan. That's doable, but the middle child would grow straight up into the space DELEGATE52's and UserLM's subtrees use, so I'd need to adjust spacing and check it visually. It's more work for a tree that's otherwise fine.

**2. Babysitting AI Agents:** skip for now.

**3. DeepTRACE:** add as a child of `answer_engine_eval` (ICLR 2026).

**4. UserLM-2.0:** fair, that was my mistake. I ranked it as optional when it's clearly the direct follow-up. It goes as a child of `userlm` with the short title "UserLM-2.0", venue arXiv.

**5. DELEGATE52 and the "just planted" sign:** change the venue to COLM 2026, and move `data-latest` (which places the "just planted" sign) to UserLM-2.0.

**6. AI-Slop to AI-Polish:** change the venue to COLM 2025.

**7. Attribution Gradients under DiverseSumm:** that fits better than my suggestion, since it's about how people read and examine sources. It goes as a child of `diverse_summ`, with indirect links to `answer_engine_eval` and DeepTRACE. One side effect: the Reading branch is labelled "2016-2023", so I'd change that to "2016-now".

If you're good with (a) for #1, I'll make all the edits. I'll draft the summaries in your style from the abstracts, list the arXiv IDs for you to check, and render the page to make sure nothing overlaps.</text>
  </turn>
