    <text>I've rebuilt the garden layout: a paper can now have any number of children, and the garden looks noticeably nicer. All your paper updates are in too. I checked it by rendering the page in headless Chrome. Nothing is committed yet.

**Layout ([garden.js](garden.js))**
- **Any number of children.** Each label's width is measured, and subtrees are packed as close as they can go without text overlapping. With an odd number of children, the middle one grows straight up, so Evolving User Intent sits directly above Lost in Conversation, between DELEGATE52 and UserLM.
- **Sizes itself.** Plant spacing and garden height come from the trees. The Reading plant is now seven flowers tall, which would have run past the top of the old fixed 580px canvas.
- **Labels pick their own side:** the leftmost children label to the left, the rest to the right. Your `data-is-left-child` attributes still force a label to the left.
- **Dashed links no longer depend on order.** A paper's indirect link to one listed after it (like Attribution Gradients → DeepTRACE) is still drawn.

**Look ([garden.css](garden.css))**
- Curved stems that taper with height, a small leaf on each stem, and haloed labels that stay readable over the dashed lines.
- Dashed links curve upward instead of being straight lines.
- Two layers of hills with grass tufts, softly drifting clouds (turned off if the visitor has reduced motion enabled) and a faint sun glow.
- Hovering a flower highlights its line of ancestors back to the root.
- The "Just planted!" sign is now drawn by garden.js from `data-latest`. The ~55 lines of sign code in index.html are gone.

**Papers ([index.html](index.html))**
- Added **Evolving User Intent** (middle child of Lost in Conversation), **UserLM-2.0** (child of UserLM, now carrying the "Just planted!" sign), **DeepTRACE** (ICLR2026, child of Answer Engine Eval) and **Attribution Gradients** (UIST2026, child of DiverseSumm, with dashed links to Answer Engine Eval and DeepTRACE).
- DELEGATE52 is now COLM2026, AI-Slop to AI-Polish (shown as Writing Quality Reward Models) is COLM2025, and the Reading branch is now "2016-now".

**Things to check**
- **The four new summaries are my drafts,** written in your "Neat Finding:" style from the arXiv abstracts. Please reread them, especially Attribution Gradients ([arXiv 2510.00361](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.00361)): I couldn't read that paper's full abstract, so its summary rests on search-result descriptions.
- **No code, data or model links on the new entries.** I didn't find any; UserLM-2.0 says the model is released but gives no URL.
- **Venues for the new papers:** Evolving Intent and UserLM-2.0 are marked arXiv, and I took ICLR2026 for DeepTRACE and UIST2026 for Attribution Gradients from Scholar.
- **[simple_garden.html](simple_garden.html)** (your public template) still renders correctly with the new code. It loads `garden.js?v=2`, which returning visitors may have cached, so you could bump that to `v=4` as I did in index.html.
- **An untracked `.traces/` folder** showed up in the repo. I didn't create it on purpose, so I've left it alone.

Want me to commit this?

Sources:
- [Attribution Gradients (arXiv 2510.00361)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.00361)
- [LLMs Get Lost in Evolving User Intent (arXiv 2607.20734)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.20734)
- [DeepTRACE (arXiv 2509.04499)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.04499)
- [Towards User Simulators That Stay On Task (arXiv 2610.31512)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.31512)</text>
