    <text>The garden is now about 1775px wide, down from about 2585px before wrapping. That's close to the original fixed 1700px, even with four more papers in it. Refresh http://localhost:8000/ to see it; I changed the script version, so a normal refresh is enough.

- **Wrapping:** any title wider than about 125px splits onto two lines, at whichever word break gives the most even pair (e.g. "Summary of / a Haystack"). The venue goes on the line below. Short titles like SWiPE and MiniCheck stay on one line.
- **Spacing:** I tightened the gap between labels and lines slightly, and the "Just planted!" sign now sits under the last line of its label.
- **Manual breaks:** if you don't like where a title breaks, put a `\n` in `data-title` and that break is used instead.

To make it narrower still, change `max_title_width` near the top of [garden.js](garden.js). At around 100, more titles wrap and labels get taller; I'd stop there, because labels stacked straight up a stem would start to crowd each other.</text>
