    <text>Here's the plan for each:

- **Wooden stakes:** each plant's name goes on a wooden board on posts at the base of its root stem, so the plant looks like it grows from behind its sign.
- **Title:** the title moves into the sky as a large cloud. It gets placed automatically in the emptiest stretch of sky, which is currently over the two shorter plants on the left, so it uses space that's empty right now.
- **Twisting:** in a run of only-children, each step gets a gentle sway and its label switches to the other side of the stem. Labels on the same side are then two steps apart instead of one, so the vertical spacing can drop from 80px to about 64px. That makes the Reading plant roughly 100px shorter.</text>
