    <text>All three changes are in. Refresh http://localhost:8000/ to see them; I bumped the script version, so a normal refresh is enough.

- **Title cloud:** "Philippe's Research Garden" now sits on a large cloud in the sky, and the separate title band is gone. It's placed automatically in open sky nearest the middle of the screen, and the garden only grows taller if no spot is free. The small clouds keep out of its way.
- **Wooden stakes:** each plant's name and years are on a wooden board with grain, nails and two posts, sitting in front of the base of the root stem.
- **Twisting:** along a run of single-child papers, each step sways about 14px and its label switches sides. That let me cut the spacing between generations from 80px to 64px, so the garden is 624px tall instead of 725px. The tradeoff is width: it's now about 1836px wide, up from 1775px, because the chains have labels on both sides.
- **Sign:** "Just planted!" now sits above its label rather than below, so it no longer runs into the paper underneath.

I removed the three `data-is-left-child` attributes from index.html (Writing Idiosyncracies, Writing Quality Reward Models, Summary of a Haystack). They were workarounds for the old layout and would now force consecutive labels in a chain onto the same side. The option still works if you want to force a label to the left.

[simple_garden.html](simple_garden.html) gets the same cloud title and stakes, because it shares garden.js and has the same `#garden_title` element.

One thing I noticed but didn't change: the long dashed links from DeepTRACE and Answer Engine Eval. to Attribution Gradients are now the busiest part of the picture. The hover-to-reveal idea from my earlier list would fix that.</text>
