127-            data-summary="Work led by Jihoon Tack, a follow-up to Lost in Conversation. In real conversations, users don't just reveal their intent piece by piece: they also revise it, and sometimes change direction entirely. We build a framework that turns existing single-turn tasks into multi-turn conversations where the user's intent evolves, while keeping each task's original evaluation (no new annotation needed!). Neat Finding: strong single-turn performance does not transfer. Models across families show large drops once the intent evolves, and struggle to keep track of what the user currently wants."&gt;
