142-            data-summary="Work led by Omer Gul, the sequel to UserLM. User simulators face a tradeoff: prompted assistants stay on task but don't sound like real users, while specialized simulators (like UserLM-8b) sound natural but drift away from complex intents. We propose an RL recipe that jointly rewards intent adherence and naturalness, with naturalness measured by a lightweight discriminator trained adversarially alongside the simulator. Neat Finding: the resulting UserLM-2.0 produces valid conversations (on task AND natural) 46.2% of the time, vs. 14.1% for the strongest prior user simulator."&gt;
