257-            data-full-title="DeepTRACE: Auditing Deep Research AI Systems for Tracking Reliability Across Citations and Evidence"
258-            data-summary="Work led by Pranav Venkit, a follow-up to Answer Engine Eval. We turn the failure cases identified in the earlier qualitative study into an automated audit framework with eight measurable dimensions (covering the answer text, its sources, and its citations), built on statement-level decomposition and citation/factual-support matrices. We audit generative search and deep research systems (GPT-5, Perplexity, Copilot, Gemini, You.com). Neat Finding: deep research modes reduce overconfidence and cite thoroughly, but remain one-sided on debate questions and still contain many statements unsupported by their own sources: citation accuracy ranges from 40% to 80% across systems."&gt;
