351-            data-summary="Work led by Hita Kambhamettu. Citations in AI answers are only useful if readers actually check them, and checking them is costly. Attribution Gradients is a reading interface that incrementally unfolds the evidence behind each claim: supporting and contradicting excerpts, evidence counts, and even second-degree citations, all in place. Neat Finding: in a lab study, participants using the interface produced substantially higher-quality revisions of AI-generated answers."&gt;
