    <text>Here are the four entries I wrote, with what I'm unsure of in each. Everything is in [index.html](index.html), and the line links go straight to each entry.

**One thing across all four:** every summary opens with "Work led by X", which gets repetitive. Your own entries vary their openings ("What happens when…", "How good are LLMs at…") and add asides like "(oh no!)". You may want to make a couple of mine sound more like you.

### 1. Evolving User Intent: [index.html:123](index.html#L123)
- **"Work led by Jihoon Tack"** is based only on Jihoon being first author. If they were an MSR intern, you could say so, as you do for Tuhin and Pranav.
- **The Neat Finding has no number.** The abstract only says "large drops". If the paper has a headline figure like the 39% in Lost in Conversation, it would land better.
- **"No new annotation needed!"** comes from the abstract: the framework keeps each task's original evaluation.
- **Short title** "Evolving User Intent", venue arXiv.

### 2. UserLM-2.0: [index.html:138](index.html#L138)
- **"(like UserLM-8b)" is my guess.** The abstract only says "specialized simulators". Please check that this is what they compare against.
- **The 46.2% vs. 14.1%** comes from the abstract. If the "strongest prior user simulator" is UserLM-8b, saying so makes a nicer sequel story.
- **No model link.** The abstract says UserLM-2.0 is released but gives no URL. If it's on Hugging Face, add `data-links-model="…"`.
- **Name:** the text says "Omer Gul", following how you referred to them, but the coauthor list uses "Mustafa Omer Gul" from arXiv. The full name is what shows in the Hall of Friends.

### 3. DeepTRACE: [index.html:254](index.html#L254)
- **System list:** I wrote "GPT-5, Perplexity, Copilot, Gemini, You.com". The abstract mentions GPT-4.5/5 and Copilot/Bing, so trim or adjust as you like.
- **It overlaps its parent's summary.** "Eight measurable dimensions" echoes the "~8 metrics" in the Answer Engine Eval entry right below it. You might focus this one on what's new: the audit is automated, and it covers deep-research modes.
